<title>UK: European cotton market sees selective demand.</title>
<headline>European cotton market sees selective demand.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European cotton market saw selective buying for nearby delivery with Central Asian, African and Syrian types finding the greatest demand, industry sources said.</p>
<p>The long staple sector was subdued and the Eastern European market generally quiet.</p>
<p>The overall market continues to be governed by caution due to an uncertain outlook for yarn and fabric consumption.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
